# CSS design tokens

Use the variables in `src/styles/tokens.css` for spacing, type, color, radius, motion, and layout. Do not invent ad-hoc sizes like `0.35em`, `0.4em`, `22rem`, or one-off opacities when a token already exists (or a nearby token is close enough).

```css
/* ❌ BAD — magic gaps and widths */
.site-footer__source {
  gap: 0.4em;
}
.site-footer__credit {
  max-width: 40rem;
}

/* ✅ GOOD — tokens from tokens.css */
.site-footer__source {
  gap: var(--space-3xs);
}
.site-footer__credit {
  max-width: var(--content-width);
}
```

If nothing fits, **add a named token** in `tokens.css` and use that — do not sprinkle a new literal across `global.css`.

Exceptions: `0` / `auto` / `100%` / `none`, `currentColor`, and true one-offs required by the platform (e.g. `1px` hairlines, `env(safe-area-inset-*)`).
